Description: bcachefs storage plugin for Proxmox VE
 Stores container rootfs volumes as bcachefs subvolumes - folders rather than
 image files - so snapshots, rollbacks and clones are native bcachefs
 operations, and applies per-storage bcachefs IO policy (compression, replicas,
 tiering targets, checksums) straight from storage.cfg.
 .
 Container sizes are enforced with bcachefs project quotas where the filesystem
 supports them, falling back to ext4-in-a-raw-image where it does not.
 .
 This package also patches PVE::LXC so that sized container rootfs volumes can
 be placed as subvolumes, and re-applies that patch after pve-container
 upgrades. Mounting snapshots of those subvolumes is handled by
 pve-lxc-snapshot-mount, which is not bcachefs-specific and is depended on
 rather than duplicated.
